<title>USA: ALPINE SKIING-RESULTS OF MEN'S WORLD CUP GIANT SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-RESULTS OF MEN'S WORLD CUP GIANT SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>BRECKENRIDGE, Colorado 1996-11-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading unofficial results in the men's World Cup giant slalom in Breckenridge, Colorado, on Saturday (tabulate under combined two-run time, first run, second run):</p>
<p>1. Fredrik Nyberg (Sweden) 2:11.83 (1:05.56-1:06.27)</p>
<p>2. Urs Kaelin (Switzerland) 2:11.99 (1:05.11-1:06.88)</p>
<p>3. Hans Knaus (Austria) 2:12.03 (1:05.51-1:06.52)</p>
<p>4. Christian Mayer (Austria) 2:12.17 (1:05.98-1:06.19)</p>
<p>5. Kjetil Andre Aamodt (Norway) 2:12.54 (1:05.36-1:07.18)</p>
<p>6. Michael Von Gruenigen (Switzerland) 2:12.58</p>
<p>(1:06.17-1:06.41)</p>
<p>7. Lasse Kjus (Norway) 2:12.77 (1:06.28-1:06.49)</p>
<p>8. Patrick Holzer (Italy) 2:12.82 (1:05.92-1:06.90)</p>
<p>9. Steve Locher (Switzerland) 2:13.00 (1:05.55-1:07.45)</p>
<p>10. Jure Kosir (Slovenia) 2:13.17 (1:05.87-1:07.30)</p>
<p>11. Siegfried Voglreiter (Austria) 2:13.69 (1:07.60-1:06.09)</p>
<p>12. Guenther Mader (Austria) 2:13.83 (1:06.54-1:07.29)</p>
<p>13. Gerhard Koenigsrainer (Italy) 2:13.89 (1:07.10-1:06.79)</p>
<p>14. Tom Stiansen (Norway) 2:14.04 (1:05.97-1:08.07)</p>
<p>15. Paul Accola (Switzerland) 2:14.10 (l:06.76-1:07.34)</p>
<p>16. Christophe Saioni (France) 2:14.25 (1:06.50-1:07.75)</p>
<p>17. Mitja Kunc (Slovenia) 2:14.27 (1:07.22-1:07.05)</p>
<p>18. Mario Reiter (Austria) 2:14.28 (1:06.38-1:07.90)</p>
<p>19. Tobias Bernerssoi (Germany) 2:14.40 (1:07.17-1:07.23)</p>
<p>20. Ian Piccard (France) 2:14.45 (1:06.98-1:07.47)</p>
<p>The results were later declared official.</p>
